          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Semco Teak Sealer earns its reputation honestly: it is one of the easiest teak finishes to apply and to maintain, and it gives the look most teak owners want, healthy wood with nothing visibly on it. What it does not do is last a long time in harsh sun without attention.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy it if you will recoat each season, pick a tinted shade rather than Cleartone, and do the two-part clean properly the first time. If you want fewer recoats, compare it with the longer-lasting options in our teak sealer rankings before you buy.
